Finding: {"title":"check:tenant-guard CI gate is defined but never invoked by pre-push or CI workflows","severity":"HIGH","area":"Tenant-guard CI enforcement","files":["scripts/check-tenant-write-guard.ts","package.json",".husky/pre-push"],"detail":"scripts/check-tenant-write-guard.ts implements two real regression gates (derive-from-URL org guard, hardcoded PII roster) and is registered as npm run check:tenant-guard (package.json:42). Grepping .husky/pre-push and .github/workflows/*.yml for check:tenant-guard / check-tenant-write-guard returns no matches — the gate is not called from the pre-push hook or from any CI workflow.","impact":"The exact class of regression this script exists to catch (hardcoded roster, derive-from-URL missing org guard — both explicitly cited in the script's own header comment as prior incidents) can be reintroduced and merged without this check ever running.","recommendation":"Add npm run check:tenant-guard to .husky/pre-push (alongside the existing migration-journal check) and/or a CI workflow step, so it actually blocks the regressions it was built to catch.","confidence":"high"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.
